# Phase 13 — axe-core manual verification protocol

This file documents the protocol for human-driven axe-core verification on
the canonical admin pages. The agent cannot execute browser-based axe-core
verification headlessly without Playwright (which is deferred to Phase 14).
This file does NOT contain green output; instead it is a reproducible
runbook for the human verifier.

## Setup

Two terminals required (api + admin dev servers).

```bash
# Terminal 1 — api (env loaded from .env.dev)
cd packages/api
npm run dev
# Wait for: "Server listening on port 7780"

# Terminal 2 — admin
cd apps/admin
npm run dev
# Wait for: "VITE v... ready in ... ms" then note the local URL (typically http://localhost:7382)
```

The `@axe-core/react` integration was wired in Phase 13 Dispatch F at
`apps/admin/src/main.tsx`. In dev mode it surfaces axe-core results to the
browser DevTools console approximately every 1000 ms. No production overhead.

## Canonical pages to audit

For each page below: open in Chrome with DevTools console open. Wait 2-3
seconds for axe-core to scan. Capture any output at level `serious` or
`critical`. Acceptable result: zero serious or critical violations.

| # | Page | URL path | Auth required |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Login | `/login` | No |
| 2 | Dashboard (post-login landing) | `/` | Yes |
| 3 | Financials | `/financials` | Yes |
| 4 | Dispatch console | `/dispatch` | Yes |
| 5 | Data Protection Officer log | `/compliance/dpo-log` | Yes |
| 6 | Consent versions | `/compliance/consent-versions` | Yes |
| 7 | A/B tests (modal patterns) | `/ab-tests` | Yes |
| 8 | User management (table + icon-only buttons) | `/users` | Yes |

## Acceptance criterion

Zero `serious` or `critical` axe-core violations on every canonical page.
`moderate` and `minor` are allowed; record them as backlog for Phase 14
Playwright e2e to assert on programmatically.

## Recording results

Create `.ai-coder/checkpoints/logs/PHASE-13/dispatch-G/axe-baseline-result.md`
with one row per page. Format:

```markdown
| Page | Critical | Serious | Moderate | Minor | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Login | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | Logo lacks alt; outlined ok |
| Dashboard | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | clean |
| ... | | | | | |
```

## Status

This dispatch (Dispatch G) does NOT include the manual verification
result. The wire-up is shipped, the protocol is documented, and the
acceptance criterion is defined. Per LAUNCH-LIMITATIONS §18, automated
full-page a11y assertion is deferred to Phase 14 Playwright e2e. This
manual audit is the interim safeguard.

## Why not headless from this dispatch

- Playwright is not installed in this repo (Phase 14 scope).
- The api package's jsdom environment cannot render the full admin app
  (it pulls in router, query client, auth context, websocket clients).
- The agent has no UI driver session in this environment.

The `packages/api/__tests__/admin-a11y-baseline.test.tsx` test (4
canonical patterns) shipped in Dispatch G IS the automated component of
the a11y baseline for this phase. It runs in jest-axe + jsdom and
asserts that the patterns the F sweep applied are actually accessible.

It is intentionally NOT a fake green for full-page rendering. The
honest claim is: pattern-level a11y is automated and PASS; full-page
a11y is human-protocol-only this phase, automated in Phase 14.

## When the human runs this protocol

Before any pre-launch QA cycle, and again after any UI change that
crosses ≥10 admin controls. Record results in `axe-baseline-result.md`
as above and commit alongside the change.
